Financial Performance – Rory
Rory's contribution to VSaaS Gating supports longer-term engineering efficiency and helps reduce technical debt across the organisation. By helping teams adopt image hard gating, we are encouraging earlier remediation of outdated and unsupported base images, rather than allowing technical debt to accumulate.
This will help development teams move towards a more proactive approach to container maintenance, regularly rebuilding images with updated base images, security fixes and other necessary updates. Over time, this should reduce the effort and complexity associated with large-scale upgrades, improve maintainability and avoid the additional costs of addressing accumulated technical debt.
I would like Rory to continue supporting the adoption and maturity of VSaaS Gating, while also looking for opportunities to improve automation and reduce manual effort across our Container Security processes.
Another area where I see an opportunity for Rory to contribute further is working with the SRE team to deliver dashboards that demonstrate the impact of the capabilities we provide to application teams. The Gating dashboard is one example, giving us better visibility of the progress and benefits we are delivering through image scanning and gating.
As he takes on this work, I would encourage Rory to make good use of the SRE team's expertise, agree clear responsibilities and coordinate activities to keep delivery moving. This will help us get more from our partnership with SRE while allowing Rory to focus on leading his workstreams and gradually take on a broader portfolio of responsibilities.


